-# The identifiers a librarian looks a person up by elsewhere. `accounts` is
-# nil when the read failed, and empty before the person's first sign-in.
%dl.admin-registry-form__readout
  %dt
    %i.fa-solid.fa-id-card{'aria-hidden' => 'true'}
    NUID
  %dd
    %span.admin-registry-table__id= nuid
  %dt
    %i.fa-solid.fa-right-to-bracket{'aria-hidden' => 'true'}
    Name at sign-in
  %dd
    - if accounts.nil?
      %span.text-muted The sign-in name could not be loaded. Try again in a moment.
    - elsif accounts.empty?
      %span.text-muted Not signed in yet.
    - else
      - accounts.each do |account|
        .admin-registry-form__readout-line
          = account['name'].presence || 'No name supplied'
          %span.admin-registry-table__id= account['email']
      .admin-registry-form__hint From the university’s authentication system. It updates at each sign-in and cannot be edited here.
